  "articleBody": "Small nail holes are easy weekend fixes, but larger remodeling projects call for experienced hands. Here are the signs it is time to bring in a professional contractor.\n\n- Water leaks or hidden moisture: Water stains on ceilings or soft drywall usually point to plumbing or roof issues that require proper remediation and drying.\n- Moving walls or opening chases: Shifting interior layouts requires carefully cutting drywall without severing electrical wires or hidden plumbing lines.\n- Sagging or bowing ceiling drywall: A dipping ceiling may indicate loose fasteners, water weight, or structural deflection requiring structural checks.\n- Difficult texture matching: Knockdown, orange peel, or smooth Level 5 finishes demand specific tools and spraying techniques to blend without obvious patch lines.\n- Wall alterations tied to larger remodels: Kitchen and bath updates need seamless coordination between framing, plumbing, drywall, and finish carpentry.\n\nWhen Professional Guidance Helps\nA hands-on general contractor can evaluate framing, verify that indoor moisture levels are controlled, and coordinate trade work so your walls finish clean.\n\nIf you are facing extensive wall repairs or planning a remodel across the Denver metro, call HH Remodeling LLC at 303-505-0866 to schedule an on-site look.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
}